ok - a live sailor serving the model passes check after one probe of <endpoint>/models
ok - the probe URL joins an endpoint with a trailing slash cleanly
ok - a placeholder sailor is refused before anything is probed, even if its address answers
ok - a sailor whose endpoint does not answer is refused
ok - a sailor whose endpoint does not list the model is refused
ok - a model outside the sailor's list and an unknown sailor are refused without a probe
ok - capacity counts live task records per sailor and excludes the task being relaunched
ok - provider-json prints the OpenCode provider entry for exactly that sailor and model
ok - validate is silent without sailors, names the first problem otherwise, and check stops on an invalid map
ok - check says whether the model is loaded or only listed, and never loads it
ok - status shows each sailor's answer, tasks, server queue, and every model as loaded, unloaded, listed, or missing
ok - set-model --replace moves every rule and default profile of that sailor, leaves other sailors alone, and keeps a dated backup
ok - set-model refuses an unserved model, a failed warm-up, a replace under a running task, and misplaced flags, writing nothing, and --dry-run only prints
ok - set-model tells a loaded model from one the server only lists, and --warm loads it
ok - in a Privateer home set-model --first-mate moves the first mate's line, and any change the quarantine would report is refused
ok - in a Privateer home the first mate's sailor cannot be parked, and only changes to what the first mate uses ask for a restart
ok - retire refuses a sailor with a task on it, and otherwise removes it, its profiles, and every rule or default left empty
ok - add registers a placeholder with the given fields and refuses a taken or malformed one; set changes only the given fields
ok - add --from-mlx-serve takes the endpoint and live models from servers.json and the server, never writing the registry or touching the server
